.Dd 2026-10-06
.Dt tmpmail 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tmpmail
.Nd temporary email
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -version
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar PROVIDER
.Fl g Op Ar ADDRESS | USERNAME
.Nm
.Op Fl t | b Ar BROWSER
.Fl r | Ar ID
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a command line utility written in POSIX shell that allows you to create a temporary email address and receive emails to the temporary email address. It receives emails through the Guerrilla Mail API, or the mail.tm API when selected with
.Fl p .
.Ss Options and Arguments
When called with no option and no argument,
.Nm
lists the messages in the inbox and their numbers.
When called with one argument,
.Nm
shows the email message with that number
.Ar ID ,
where 1 is the newest.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b , Fl Fl browser Ar BROWSER
Specify
.Ar BROWSER
(default: w3m) that is used to render the HTML of the email
.It Fl Fl clipboard-cmd Ar COMMAND
Specify the COMMAND to use for copying the email address to your
clipboard (default: xclip -selection c)
.It Fl c , Fl Fl copy
Copy the email address to your clipboard
.It Fl d , Fl Fl domains
Show list of available domains
.It Fl g , Fl Fl generate Op Ar ADDRESS | USERNAME
Generate a new email address, either the specified
.Ar ADDRESS ,
a
.Ar USERNAME
on a random domain, or a completely random one
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Show help
.It Fl p , Fl Fl provider Ar PROVIDER
Service used for new addresses:
.Cm guerrilla
(default) or
.Cm mailtm .
Can also be set with the
.Ev TMPMAIL_PROVIDER
environment variable.
An existing address keeps the provider it was made with.
.It Fl r , Fl Fl recent
View the most recent email message
.It Fl t , Fl Fl text
View the email as raw text, where all the HTML tags are removed.  Without this option, HTML is used.
.It Fl Fl version
Show version
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev TMPMAIL_PROVIDER
Default provider for new addresses,
.Cm guerrilla
or
.Cm mailtm .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /tmp/tmpmail
The current address, its provider, the mail.tm password, the last viewed email and downloaded attachments.
.El
